      "description": "Watch Cardiff City vs Norwich highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The atmosphere was electric on 2026-08-25 as Cardiff City and Norwich City faced off in a high-stakes Carabao Cup encounter. Both teams took to the pitch with everything to play for, setting the stage for a classic cup tie full of tactical intrigue. Canaries Take Flight Early Norwich City began the match with intent, dictating the tempo and looking to exploit gaps in the Cardiff City defense. Their persistence paid off in the 25th minute when a well-delivered corner from Jacob Wright found Mathias Kvistgaarden . The forward rose highest in the center of the box to power a header into the high center of the goal, giving the visitors a deserved lead. Cardiff attempted to claw their way back before the break, with Callum Robinson testing Daniel Grimshaw from distance, but the Canaries went into halftime with their advantage intact. Early in the second half, Norwich nearly doubled their lead as Anis Ben Slimane saw his header rattle the crossbar in the 49th minute. Seeking a spark, Cardiff made a triple substitution in the 67th minute, introducing Yousef Salech , Jack Moylan , and Cian Ashford . The changes briefly shifted momentum, and David Turnbull forced another fine save from Grimshaw , but the clinical edge belonged to the visitors. Late Drama and the Final Blow As the game moved into its final stages, Norwich City appeared to put the result beyond doubt. In the 78th minute, Jack Stacey set up Ante Crnac , who clinicaly placed a left-footed shot into the center of the goal to make it 2-0. It felt like a knockout blow, but the Bluebirds refused to go quietly into the night. Deep into stoppage time, in the 93rd minute, Yousef Salech latched onto a pass from Rob Tankiewicz and fired a brilliant left-footed strike into the top left corner. The late goal sparked a frantic final few minutes as Cardiff threw everything forward, but the referee's final whistle confirmed a 2-1 victory for Norwich City , who progress to the next round after a hard-fought battle in South Wales."
